<section class="isnad-dilemma" aria-labelledby="isnad-dilemma-title">
    <div class="isnad-dilemma__head">
        <p class="isnad-dilemma__eyebrow">Transmission criticism</p>
        <h2 id="isnad-dilemma-title">The Isnād Dilemma</h2>
        <p>When five hundred witnesses become one chain.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="isnad-dilemma__grid">
        <article class="dilemma-panel">
            <header class="dilemma-panel__header">
                <span class="dilemma-panel__icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
                <div>
                    <p>Analogy</p>
                    <h3>Courtroom Scenario</h3>
                </div>
            </header>

            <div class="dilemma-quote">
                <span>Witness testifies</span>
                <blockquote>
                    “Your Honor, five hundred people saw the defendant commit
                    the crime.”
                </blockquote>
            </div>

            <div class="dilemma-flow">
                <div class="dilemma-source">
                    <span>Single</span>
                    <strong>Witness</strong>
                </div>

                <div class="dilemma-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

                <div class="dilemma-claim">
                    <strong>Claims five hundred others told him</strong>
                    <div class="dot-grid" aria-hidden="true">
                        {Array.from({ length: 50 }).map(() => <i />)}
                    </div>
                    <em>But none appear in court.</em>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="dilemma-equation">
                <span>1 Witness</span>
                <b>+</b>
                <span>500 Testimonies</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dilemma-verdict">
                <span>Legally</span>
                <strong>Still just one witness</strong>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="dilemma-panel dilemma-panel--resurrection">
            <header class="dilemma-panel__header">
                <span class="dilemma-panel__icon" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>
                <div>
                    <p>Claim</p>
                    <h3>Resurrection Claim</h3>
                </div>
            </header>

            <div class="dilemma-quote">
                <span>Paul writes</span>
                <blockquote>
                    “Christ appeared to more than five hundred brothers at
                    once.”
                </blockquote>
            </div>

            <div class="dilemma-flow">
                <div class="dilemma-source">
                    <span>Single</span>
                    <strong>Source</strong>
                    <small>Paul</small>
                </div>

                <div class="dilemma-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

                <div class="dilemma-claim">
                    <strong>Claims five hundred others saw Jesus</strong>
                    <div class="dot-grid" aria-hidden="true">
                        {Array.from({ length: 50 }).map(() => <i />)}
                    </div>
                    <em>But no independent chains exist.</em>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="dilemma-equation">
                <span>1 Isnād</span>
                <b>+</b>
                <span>500 Attestations</span>
            </div>

            <div class="dilemma-verdict dilemma-verdict--historical">
                <span>Historically</span>
                <strong>Still just one chain</strong>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>

    <aside class="method-irony">
        <div class="method-irony__mark" aria-hidden="true">◇</div>

        <div>
            <p class="isnad-dilemma__eyebrow">The methodological irony</p>
            <h3>
                Five hundred unnamed witnesses do not become five hundred
                independent testimonies.
            </h3>
            <p>
                Christian polemicists dismiss isnād criticism as too demanding
                for ancient history, yet their own central claim fails even this
                basic standard. The number sounds large, but historically the
                evidence still comes through one recoverable source.
            </p>
            <strong>
                If the only recoverable witness is one chain, then the
                historical evidence remains one chain.
            </strong>
        </div>
    </aside>
</section>

